<title>PORTUGAL: World mine/refined copper output up in Jan-April.</title>
<headline>World mine/refined copper output up in Jan-April.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>World mine and refined copper production rose in the first four months of the year, according to the International Copper Study Group's (ICSG) latest bulletin.</p>
<p>The ICSG said mine output was up 3.7 percent while refined copper rose 5.6 percent in January-April compared with the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>For the month of April the market was almost in balance with consumption only marginally higher than production.</p>
<p>The ICSG said the average London Metal Exchange (LME) spot price for May was $2,514 per tonne, compared with $2,390 in April.</p>
<p>The following figures are expressed in thousand tonnes unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>				   April 97   March 97   Jan-April 97</p>
<p>World consumption	    1,121	1,111	4,406</p>
<p>World mine capacity	  1,044	1,044	3,133</p>
<p>World mine production	  931	  928	3,613</p>
<p>Percent capacity utilisation  89.1	 88.9	115.3</p>
<p>Primary refined production   926	  909	3,612</p>
<p>Secondary refined production 191	  197	  765</p>
<p>Total refined</p>
<p>production		     1,117	1,106	4,377</p>
<p>Percent scrap in total</p>
<p>refined production		17.1	 17.8	 17.5</p>
<p>Refined stocks</p>
<p>end of period		    649	  679	  649</p>
<p>Refined deficit		    5	    5	   29</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
